      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "why does vrchat have to be responsible for a parent's inability to parent? \"this is like blaming the knife company for making the knife sharp, when a kid got cut with a kitchen knife.\nTwo options comes:\n1. How to make the knife less sharp for kids\n2. A responsible adult should put the knife in a safe place out of reach\"\nchildren being on vrchat has been a problem for a long time (staff knows. these posts beat a dead horse and waste time), especially since the quest 2 is affordable VR but nobody seems to be able to wrap their head around the fact that vrchat can't police someone's age.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
