      "value": "@{62799be879611c5288c560eb|full_name}: \nOfc It isn’t VRChats task to police their age let alone is it possible.\nBut what about VRChat giving the parents the possibility to police their children?\ni mean let me ask you this: \nHow can you parent your children in a game that doesn’t give the options to restrict certain access\nNo matter how well you are parented as a kid wouldn’t you be curious on breaking the rules or test out how far you can go? Ofc most kids would do that. That’s how children are and that’s good! \nImo giving the parents the option and opportunity to limit the things the kids can do in vr, Will encourage parents to parent their children without the kids completely being forbidden (what VRChat is scared of). \nAlso regarding the example with the knife factory You are forgetting a major point on this:\nParents know how sharp knives can be! \nThey *dont* know how dangerous vr is as it is something very new. You can see enough little children when browsing through social media.\nOfc there are some with parents not caring of what they are doing online and all in all not caring about their children. But please don’t see it as all parents are like that. There is also a huge amount of parents not really understanding the aspects social media (and even more for VR) can bring. Those parents often think: „my kid grew up with this shit so they should know the best“ which is a big misconception.\nGiving the option to take measurements on parental control gives lots of parents the hint: „mhh there might be a reason for that to exist“ instead of not caring or not understanding the risks",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
