      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "EDIT:\nJust to give a clarification on my suggestion/theory.\n- Parents are able to set their children accounts as so called “Kids Accounts” (maybe on the website so they don’t even need to go in VR)\n- It is up to the parents to set this limit of the kids account for their children!\n- There would be a new toggle in the world upload and instances creation menu named “Content for Children” (For example) \n- Worlds and especially instances which are seen as “Content for children” do not change anything to a normal public lobby at the moment\n- you’d need to specifically create an instance or world not suitable for children\n- creating such a world/instance would have some big drawbacks (still unknown) so not everyone would create such instances\n- Children with “Kids Accounts” wont be able to see these Instances/Worlds (for example an instance of some people having drinking games)\n- MAYBE hiding avatars with the NSFW tag given on upload (but i wouldn’t consider that as a major issue as i see a bigger problem with some worlds & people behind those avatars)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
