  "details": "I've seen this discusion popping up a lot in the the past month of adding NSFW or 18+ filter to worlds or instances and i have to agree that VRChat wont take action in that part as it would mean, they would aknowlege 18+ Content existing in their Game.\nSo here is a Suggestion of me on how to bypass this dilemma:\nGive Parents the option to set the Account of their children as a \"Kids Account\" that will prevent them from joining certain worlds.\nTo filter out worlds you could either add a checkbox on the World upload that sets the tag \"Content for children\" or have a checkbox on instance creation to disable it showing for children with \"Kids Accounts\".\nThis will definetly not solve the whole Problem, but it will make some Parents aware that their children might get inflicted with not appropriate content for children without VRChat itself aknowledging NSFW & 18+ Stuff happening on this Game\nA decent side Benifit would be a more positve light of some Media outlets as it would ease them a little to see VRChat taking actions against the current sexual exposure that some minors are confronted in the Game.",
